# Size survey 2026-10-10 (optimization `literal-consts`): 1000 and 100000 reads of a literal constant in a loop.
# Natively a closed term is made once and a read allocates nothing; lean2rr's literal cache makes the string at the
# first read only. A read that made the string every time would allocate 99000 times more at the large size.
1000 | 100000 | 1 50
